PARSFILE
#FullDataName Events`AEB CCRm,s C. Check More Tests`Euro NCAP AEB Testing
#CheckBox1 1    
*CLEAR
#CheckBox6 0    
#CheckBox7 0    
#CheckBox9 0    
#CheckBox10 0    

#RingCtrl0 <=
#RingCtrl1 >
#RingCtrl10 2
#RingCtrl11 4
RESET_EVENTS
*NAME1 Crashed
*NAME2 Crashed
*VALUE1 0
*VALUE2 0
MAKE_EVENT Crashed <= 0 ; Events\Events_2c07d17a-44e6-4af9-96ae-093b38b2633d.par
#BlueLink0 Events`AEB CCRm,s E. New Test, Increase Speed` Euro NCAP AEB Testing` , Events`Events_2c07d17a-44e6-4af9-96ae-093b38b2633d

MAKE_EVENT Crashed > 0 ; Events\Events_850c1411-e276-4b75-a833-0b8e200f164c.par
#BlueLink1 Events`AEB CCRm,s D. Pause before ending` Euro NCAP AEB Testing` , Events`Events_850c1411-e276-4b75-a833-0b8e200f164c

SET_EVENT_ID 0 ! reset to default

#EMBEDDED_NOTES
#If the variable Crashed is not zero, we're done
#- The vehicle has previously contacted the target, and did not contact it on this run, so that is the formal end of the test
#
#If the  variable Crashed is zero, increase the test speed, and try the test again at the new higher speed
#
#
#END_EMBEDDED_NOTES

LOG_ENTRY Used Dataset: Events; { Euro NCAP AEB Testing } AEB CCRm,s C. Check More Tests
